From fc842aa4bc36a605febd6733f7c26f838ae7611e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JorreFog <JorreFog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:34:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] Eleven more shaders, from libretro's glsl-shaders (for
 SuperDrastic and BananaDS)

lcd1x-nds, lcd1x, lcd3x, nds-color, zfast-lcd, retro-v2, bevel,
sharp-bilinear, sharp-bilinear-scanlines, zfast-crt, fxaa: libretro's
single-pass shaders converted to this project's interface by
tools/shaders/conv.py (the fragment stage; libretro's names mapped onto
u_texture, u_texture_size, u_output_size, v_texcoord; SWIZ on the
result), each keeping its original notice (THIRD_PARTY.md).

Chosen by fit and cost on the RG DS's GPU at 600 MHz (a 512x384 screen
drawn to 640x480): 1.1-3.3 ms a screen. Left out: aann, crt-easymode,
pixel-art-aa, pixellate (5.7-9.7 ms a screen), crt-pi, crt-lottes-fast,
crt-aperture, scanline, grade (don't compile for GLSL ES 1.00), quilez
(no licence notice).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SoPzircPRmhYJPUYUWuUMW
(cherry picked from commit adbf916e74f6d0dcb36778e0bbb69cb3a2059059)
