From: JorreFog <JorreFog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:28:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] shaders: ds-grid's grid on the RG DS thin and even (no
 thick bars, no 2px/3px cells)

At 2.5 panel pixels per DS pixel the grid was one whole snapped pixel at 0.42 (linear) plus a
neighbour at 0.72: about 2 of every 2.5 pixels darkened, line pixels at 0, 2, 5, 7, 10..., so
cells alternated 2 and 3 pixels and lost different light (34% spread between cells, beat 0.66 of
the grid's own amplitude, measured on the panel).

Now each axis's darkening is GRID_DARKNESS * (1 + cos) peaking on the DS-pixel boundaries: the
band-limited form of a thin gap. Every cell loses the same light, no period-5 beat (0.02 on the
panel), darkest pixel 0.82 of the flat colour, the pixel pairs 0.90. GRID_CRISP > 0 mixes in a
sharp GAP_WIDTH gap by area coverage (crisper, with a faint plaid). Whole-number scales (the RG DS
Plus) keep the old snapped grid, pixel for pixel. ds-grid-color regenerated.

